<div class="document-body"><h2>How to use this pack</h2>
<p>This controlled pack brings together the records and procedures that are required, likely required, or strongly indicated for Aimee’s current processing. Each numbered section is intended to operate as a separate controlled document even though the material is packaged in one editable file.</p>
<div class="callout warning">Immediate deployment gates<br>Do not represent Aimee as fully compliant until the actions marked CRITICAL are complete. In particular: (1) highly effective age assurance must protect UK access to adult/pornographic output; (2) separate explicit-consent controls must cover special-category processing and optional human quality review; (3) processor contracts, transfer safeguards and retention configuration must be verified; and (4) a working privacy complaints channel must be assigned and tested.</div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="policy-table"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Controlled document</th><th>Status in law/governance</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Governance and document register</td><td>Required accountability control</td><td>Director approval</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Data Protection Impact Assessment</td><td>Likely legally required before high-risk AI processing</td><td>Complete actions and sign off</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Record of Processing Activities and data map</td><td>Required because processing is non-occasional and includes high-risk/special-category data</td><td>Maintain continuously</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Lawful basis record and Legitimate Interests Assessments</td><td>Required evidence where legitimate interests are relied upon</td><td>Legal review</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Appropriate Policy Document</td><td>Required for relevant DPA 2018 Schedule 1 conditions</td><td>Adopt before safeguarding processing under those conditions</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Retention and deletion schedule</td><td>Required to demonstrate storage limitation and support APD</td><td>Configure deletion jobs</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Senior human-review and access-control policy</td><td>Strong governance control for intimate transcripts</td><td>Adopt and train reviewers</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Safeguarding and escalation policy</td><td>Necessary operational safety control</td><td>Appoint Safeguarding Lead</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Data subject rights and complaints procedure</td><td>Rights procedure required; formal complaints process mandatory from 19 June 2026</td><td>Deploy electronic channel</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Personal data breach response plan</td><td>Required accountability and breach-response control</td><td>Test tabletop exercise</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Processor and international-transfer register</td><td>Required Article 28 and Chapter V governance</td><td>Complete vendor due diligence</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Age assurance and adult-content compliance record</td><td>Ofcom / Online Safety Act control where adult content can be generated</td><td>CRITICAL before adult route is available</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Consent and just-in-time transparency standard</td><td>Required to make explicit consent valid and transparent</td><td>Build into onboarding/settings</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>1. Governance and controlled-document register</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="policy-table"><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Approved position</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Legal controller</td><td>Ampera EV Ltd, trading through its Engram Intelligence brand</td></tr><tr><td>Company number</td><td>16439998</td></tr><tr><td>Registered office</td><td>34–40 Witham, Witham, Hull, England, HU9 1BY</td></tr><tr><td>Data Protection Lead</td><td>[TO COMPLETE: dedicated privacy email address]</td></tr><tr><td>ICO registration</td><td>[TO COMPLETE: ICO registration number, if registered]</td></tr><tr><td>Board / director owner</td><td>[TO COMPLETE]</td></tr><tr><td>Senior Safeguarding Lead</td><td>[TO COMPLETE]</td></tr><tr><td>Technical system owner</td><td>[TO COMPLETE]</td></tr><tr><td>Review frequency</td><td>At least every six months, and after material model, provider, safety or legal changes</td></tr><tr><td>Document status</td><td>Draft v1.0 – not yet approved</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2>Roles and accountability</h2>
<ul>
<li>Director / Board owner: accepts residual risk, approves lawful bases, resources controls and signs the DPIA.</li>
<li>Data Protection Lead: maintains the ROPA, privacy notice, complaints process, rights requests, breach log and processor register.</li>
<li>Senior Safeguarding Lead: owns escalation decisions, external disclosures, reviewer training and case quality.</li>
<li>HQ Directors: approve senior reviewer access and identity-reveal requests under the governed Aimee HQ workflow.</li>
<li>Senior Safeguarding reviewers: conduct proportionate, purpose-limited reviews under timed sessions and audited access.</li>
<li>Technical owner: implements access controls, pseudonymisation, deletion, logging, provider configuration and incident containment.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Change control</h2>
<p>A new DPIA review and policy update is required before any material change to model providers, erotic/adult functionality, age assurance, human review scope, data categories, retention, international transfers, biometric identification, location use, autonomous messaging or external disclosure arrangements.</p></div>
